NVIDIA CUDA runtime and cuBLAS

A Singularity build whose local inference runs on NVIDIA GPUs carries these
NVIDIA components inside its llama.cpp runtime, and only there:

- the CUDA runtime (cudart), linked statically into llama-server;
- cuBLAS (cublas64_<major>.dll and cublasLt64_<major>.dll on Windows), which
  llama-server loads and which ship beside it in llama.cpp/, as the NVIDIA
  CUDA Toolkit End User License Agreement lists them as redistributable
  (Attachment A).

The NVIDIA display driver (nvcuda.dll, libcuda.so.1) and its management
library (nvml.dll, libnvidia-ml.so.1) are the computer's own: Singularity loads
them at run time and never redistributes them.

